132
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:48,000
You guys all have the experience

133
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:50,000
of having worked in Cub Scouting,

134
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:52,000
making the transition up to Boy Scouts.

135
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:55,000
What kind of person makes a good Scoutmaster?

136
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:57,000
And I'll turn to you first, Larry.

137
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:59,000
I think a lot of Scoutmasters

138
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:03,000
are kind of in a middle position somewhere.

139
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:09,000
They're not usually CEOs or guys that are really, really busy.

140
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:13,000
It's usually somebody that understands leadership

141
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:14,000
and can do some of that,

142
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:16,000
but is not necessarily a business owner

143
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:20,000
or somebody that's so busy they don't have time for it.

144
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:26,000
And then it's somebody that loves working with Scouts,

145
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:29,000
that wants to really get in there, either with their own son

146
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:31,000
or with- if they don't have a son-

147
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:33,000
somebody that really wants to work with them

148
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:34,000
and to learn and to grow.

149
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:36,000
What would you add to that, Tom?

150
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:42,000
Well, the person would have to be willing to try different things,

151
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:45,000
to go a little bit outside his comfort zone,

152
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:48,000
get out of the box type stuff.

153
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:49,000
